bash ~/start_nav2_minimal.sh 




1. Replace hardcoded box positions with vision detections (the big one)
  Right now autonomous_[mission.py](http://mission.py) has BOX_POSITIONS = {...} baked in. Have
  vision publish a topic like /detected_boxes (custom msg or                    
  visualization_msgs/MarkerArray) carrying:
  - name (red_box_1, etc.)                                                      
  - world_x, world_y, color                                                     
                           
  Mission subscribes and uses live detections instead of the dictionary. Then if
   you move boxes around, the rover finds them on its own. This is the main     
  thing.
                                                                                
  2. Color verification before pickup                                           
  After the rover stops at the approach pose, vision checks the camera frame for
   the expected color. If it doesn't see red where it should, abort/retry       
  instead of grabbing the wrong box.                        
                                                                                
  3. Detect successful drop in basket                                           
  After place, point the camera at the basket. Vision confirms the colored box
  is in. If not (e.g., it bounced out), command a retry or log failure.         
                                                            
  4. Color-based routing for unknown boxes                                      
  If a box appears in the room without a known label (e.g., user spawns
  "red_box_99"), vision sees "this is red" and the mission routes it to the red 
  basket. No code change needed for new boxes.
                                                                                
  5. Real-time obstacle classification                                          
  Vision detects pedestals from the camera and feeds them to the costmap as
  obstacles — solves the "lidar can't see short pedestals" problem we've been   
  fighting.                                                 
                                                                                
  6. The keypress UI as a HMI on top                                            
  Keep the keypress window but route it through the mission, not Nav2 directly.
  Press 'r' → mission switches its queue to "all red boxes first." Avoids the   
  action-server conflict.                                   
                                                                                
  Tell your friend the most impactful target is #1: a /detected_boxes topic that
   the mission subscribes to. I can wire the mission side once they have a
  stable detection topic — just need the message type and the topic name. 

